cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spi in your work, please cite it using the citation below."
type: software

title: "spi: Bayesian Spatiotemporal Modelling of Relative AFP Reporting"
version: 0.0.0.9000

abstract: >-
  An R package for estimating district-level relative acute flaccid paralysis
  (AFP) reporting. spi models expected non-polio AFP (NPAFP) counts by district
  and month using Bayesian spatiotemporal models fitted with INLA, then compares
  observed and expected counts through the Surveillance Performance Index (SPI).
  By default, district observed-to-expected ratios are centred on the national
  observed-to-expected ratio for the same period. The package provides posterior
  uncertainty, diagnostic plots, concordance with the conventional NPAFP rate,
  and tools for district-level surveillance review.

